"## Summary\n\nDevstack follow-up 34: F30-01's acceptance proof, r29's L-2, and wire-nodes 35's hand-off.\n- **Session:** launched 00:32 EST on 2026-11-04 on #454's roadmap row `33f0ef8e`, and delivered at 01:36.\n- **Model:** codex `gpt-6-astra`.\n- **Size:** 4 commits and 115 owned files, +50,413/−17. Almost all of it is the run's records under `docs/e2e/runs/2026-11-04/followup34/`.\n- **Checks:**\n  - merges cleanly onto current `main`; prepush-scan clean; owned-check passes.\n  - **The orchestrator reran these** on a scratch tree: current `main` with this branch and isolation 22 merged in. All pass:\n    - `make -f mk/e2e.mk e2e-lint`, and `make -f mk/at-isolation.mk at-isolation-lint at-isolation-test at-isolation-build`;\n    - `go vet -tags e2e ./tests/e2e/...`, which compiles every AT package;\n    - `go test ./tests/e2e/...`, including the nine `TestD144_` nightly gate tests on the frozen and the live lists;\n    - `go test ./tests/handover/...`, including handover 43's claims, and the committed-evidence tests;\n    - `make go-lint`, gofmt and `git diff --check`.\n- **Scope:** the e2e harness's observers, the nightly list and its tests, and records. No AT file, production code or contract changed.\n\n**The orchestrator's reading.**\n- **One full acceptance run,** `af4c130b`, on updater 24 (#446), agent-core 48 (#447) and agent-core 49 (#454): **31 pass, 2 blocked, 0 fail**, make exit 2, no rerun. Only two rows changed from follow-up 29's after-full run.\n- **`lease-expiry` passes** (was blocked).\n  - `countedFlow` found admission in 244 ms.\n  - The control stop returned at 05:50:52Z. The node kept serving, and forwarding stopped at the desired policy's deadline D, 06:00:47.41Z. The agent's `policy_expired` baseline began 32 ms after D, and its first closed heartbeat was 230 ms after D.\n  - The closed-path checks held, with senders still active: replies stayed at 1,193 TCP and 1,193 UDP, bytes stayed flat, and attempts kept rising.\n  - The control restart was ready at 06:00:57Z, and the same agent served again at 06:00:59Z.\n  - D was the desired policy's bound; the leases themselves ran longer. No packet-exact cutoff is claimed.\n- **`update-good` is newly blocked** (was pass): `fvpn-updater run` exited 3 (`ExitBusy`) before it started a candidate. `update-bad` passed, with exit 1 and `HASH_MISMATCH`.\n  - **The lock samples,** about every 215 ms, show the running agent (PID 876) holding `update.lock` in three consecutive samples at each new generation, every 5 s: 05:50:22.85–23.28Z, 27.69–28.13Z, 32.85–33.28Z and 37.83–38.26Z. Each hold lasts between 0.43 s and 0.86 s.\n  - **The updater's `withLock`** makes 5 attempts 20 ms apart, so it gives up after 80 ms. The failed attempt's instant was not captured.\n  - **So the candidate never started.** The agent's deferred boot recovery under D-155 was never exercised, and this run cannot prove it.\n- **The nightly list.**\n  - `lease-expiry`'s entry is removed, because the run passed it. `member-ipv6`'s entry stays byte-identical, so r29's L-2 stale citations leave with the removed entry.\n  - The nightly gate tests that read follow-up 29's list now read a byte-identical frozen copy, `tests/e2e/testdata/nightly_expected_blocked_followup29.json`. A new test pins the live list to the one `member-ipv6` entry.\n  - **The gate's verdict on this run is fail, before and after the edit,** on the unexpected blocked `update-good`. No entry was added for it.\n- **F30-01 stays open.** The brief's closure branch assumed that a passing `lease-expiry` follows the real candidate update. Here it did not, so the lane kept the finding open rather than close it on the wrong evidence. That was the right call.\n- **New observers** retain the lock holder and heartbeat, the poll's timing, the control stop and restart, and the closed-path samples. They read only: none takes the lock or changes a gate.\n- **Disclosed, and not timing-relevant here:**\n  - the run's window is confounded under D-